Mr. John T Jensen (comjohn@ccu1.aukuni.ac.nz) wrote:
: My 12-year old has asked me to post three questions about PC nethack (sorry,
: don't know what version he has):
: 
: 1)      He has found half a dozen or so throne rooms, killed all the
: 	monsters, and sits on the throne.  When he does, he is told
: 	"you feel out of place" and the throne disappears.  Has anyone
: 	any comment?

What happens greatly depends on the luck of your character.  I don't have
the specifics, but having really high luck (a luck stone would also help)
greatly increases your chances with a lot of things, including getting a
wish from a throne.  Throwing identified gems (not glass) to a unicorn of
your alignment (black=chaotic, grey=nuetral, white=lawful) will bring you
luck if the unicorn catches it.

: 2)	He knows how to get Excalibur, but wants to know how to get:
: -	a katana named Snickersnee
: -	a war hammer named Mjollnir
: -	a broadsword named Stormbringer

These weapons have some sort of alignment (Snickersnee and Mjollnir are
lawful, and Stormbringer is chaotic).  You can get them either by wishing
or if your alignment matches that of the weapon, if you offer enough
monsters at your altar, then eventually your god will give you a special
weapon.  It might turn out to be the one you want.

: 3)	The verb 'pray' does not give a syntax error, but 'offer' does.
: 	There are altars.  Any suggestions?

What do you mean a syntax error?  What is the message the program gives?

